-> 1.5707963267949<sep>[DETAIL]: <link><code>RADIANS( X )</code>&LINK&https://dev.mysql.com/doc/refman/8.4/mathematical-functions.html#function_radians</link>
Returns the argument <code>X</code> , converted from degrees to radians. (Note that π radians equals 180 degrees.) Returns <code>NULL</code> if <code>X</code> is <code>NULL</code> .

[DESCRIPTION]: Repeat a string the specified number of times<sep>[DEMO]: mysql> SELECT REPEAT('MySQL', 3);
-> 'MySQLMySQLMySQL'<sep>[DETAIL]: <link><code>REPEAT( str , count )</code>&LINK&https://dev.mysql.com/doc/refman/8.4/string-functions.html#function_repeat</link>
Returns a string consisting of the string <code>str</code> repeated <code>count</code> times. If <code>count</code> is less than 1, returns an empty string. Returns <code>NULL</code> if <code>str</code> or <code>count</code> is <code>NULL</code> .

example:
mysql> SELECT ROUND(-1.23);
-> -1
mysql> SELECT ROUND(-1.58);
-> -2
mysql> SELECT ROUND(1.58);
-> 2
mysql> SELECT ROUND(1.298, 1);
-> 1.3
mysql> SELECT ROUND(1.298, 0);
-> 1
mysql> SELECT ROUND(23.298, -1);
-> 20
mysql> SELECT ROUND(.12345678901234567890123456789012345, 35);
-> 0.123456789012345678901234567890

detail:
[DESCRIPTION]: Append string the specified number of times<sep>[DEMO]: mysql> SELECT RPAD('hi',5,'?');
-> 'hi???'
mysql> SELECT RPAD('hi',1,'?');
-> 'h'<sep>[DETAIL]: <link><code>RPAD( str , len , padstr )</code>&LINK&https://dev.mysql.com/doc/refman/8.4/string-functions.html#function_rpad</link>
Returns the string <code>str</code> , right-padded with the string <code>padstr</code> to a length of <code>len</code> characters. If <code>str</code> is longer than <code>len</code> , the return value is shortened to <code>len</code> characters. If <code>str</code> , <code>padstr</code> , or <code>len</code> is <code>NULL</code> , the function returns <code>NULL</code> .
This function is multibyte safe.

example:
mysql> SELECT RPAD('hi',5,'?');
-> 'hi???'
mysql> SELECT RPAD('hi',1,'?');
-> 'h'

